      "id": 1,
      "text": "William Sachse founded the town in 1845 after immigrating from Prussia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachse%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the German word for Saxon, reflecting its founder’s heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachse%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1886, Sachse donated 100 feet of land to the railroad, which built a depot that gave the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachse%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After purchasing 640 acres, Sachse erected the first cotton mills and gins in Collin County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachse%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Sachse Historical Society preserves and shares the city’s story, offering resources for researchers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
